{"id": "tea:niyamasara:187", "source": "src:niyamasara", "location": {"ref": "187"}, "paraphrase": "I have composed this scripture named Niyamasāra for the sake of my own contemplation, having heard the teaching of the Jina.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "practice"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "notes": "Concluding verse (number moderate confidence).", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:niyamasara:3", "source": "src:niyamasara", "location": {"ref": "3"}, "paraphrase": "What must be done without fail (niyama) is knowledge, perception and conduct; 'essence' (sāra) is added to exclude their opposites.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "concepts": ["cpt:three-jewels"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:niyamasara:6", "source": "src:niyamasara", "location": {"ref": "6"}, "paraphrase": "The reliable one (āpta) is free of the eighteen faults: hunger, thirst, fear, anger, attachment, delusion, anxiety, old age, disease, death, sweat, fatigue, pride, pleasure, wonder, sleep, birth and distress.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "realized"}, "types": ["ultimate", "powers-experiences"], "speaker": "Kundakunda", "concepts": ["cpt:eighteen-dosas-absent-in-jina", "cpt:kevalibhukti"], "disputes": ["dsp:kevalin-eats"], "terms": ["trm:apta"], "notes": "The Digambara list of eighteen faults, which includes hunger and thirst; exact order and verse number moderate confidence.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U34-jain-canon"], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U34-jain-canon"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
